{"name":"Ash Grove","hex":"#b9b3bf","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ash grove","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(This entry is a translation hub.)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ash_grove"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Ash Grove","blocks":[{"text":"\"The Ash Grove\" is a traditional Welsh folk song; numerous sets of lyrics have been set to its melody. The best-known English lyrics were written by Thomas Oliphant in the 19th century."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Ash_Grove","wikidata":"Q3257554"},{"title":"Ash Grove (music club)","blocks":[{"text":"The Ash Grove was a folk music club located at 8162 Melrose Avenue in Los Angeles, California, United States, founded in 1958 by Ed Pearl and named after the Welsh folk song, \"The Ash Grove\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ash_Grove_(music_club)","wikidata":"Q4804381"},{"title":"Ash","blocks":[{"text":"Ash is the solid remnants of fires. Specifically, ash refers to all non-aqueous, non-gaseous residues that remain after something burns. In analytical chemistry, to analyse the mineral and metal content of chemical samples, ash is the non-gaseous, non-liquid residue after complete combustion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Wood_ash.jpg/330px-Wood_ash.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ash","wikidata":"Q152079"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Llwyn_onn_%28The_Ash_Grove%29_page_1.jpg/250px-Llwyn_onn_%28The_Ash_Grove%29_page_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/11/Llwyn_onn_%28The_Ash_Grove%29_page_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Llwyn_onn_%28The_Ash_Grove%29_page_1.jpg/250px-Llwyn